			"date": "2023-01-09T16:28:38.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> I think it would be interesting if we forced developers to develop the site without JavaScript if they use frameworks with SSR. In my experience, CSR does make websites feel nice to use. It's a balance I guess.<br>Im considering modifying <a href=\"https://github.com/fireship-io/flamethrower\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><span class=\"invisible\">https://</span><span class=\"ellipsis\">github.com/fireship-io/flameth</span><span class=\"invisible\">rower</span></a> for my 11ty site</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
