			"date": "2023-01-09T16:29:51.374Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://social.coop/@eb\" class=\"u-url mention\">@<span>eb</span></a></span> ah hmm—what’s the accessibility story of that component?</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "109660217678337275",
			"parentId": "109660195479336854",
			"url": "https://social.coop/@eb/109660217640353441",
			"author": {
				"name": "Evan B🥥ehs",
				"url": "https://social.coop/@eb",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/403/079/868/456/691/original/f41d3e92406d02c0.jpeg"
			},
			"date": "2023-01-09T16:35:29.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> of flamethrower? I doubt there's any. It just hijacks standard links, fetches the body of the page they point to, and hotswaps that in. This should be good for performance because<br>1. Progressive Enhancement<br>2. On each click, the browser no longer needs to parse and rerun JavaScript, fonts, and styles</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "109660231753109680",
